            {
              "abbreviation": "aa",
              "hint": "Appeal to authority: Leaning on an authority counts as evidence only when the authority is real and relevant. It’s a fallacy when: (1) the person isn’t an expert on this subject; (2) the experts themselves don’t agree; (3) the conclusion claims the authority *must* be right (and isn’t just probably right).",
